version: 2.0.0
description: |
  Provider-agnostic task sync seam. TWO-WAY as of Phase 2b: local tasks project
  OUT to an external tracker AND remote changes reconcile BACK — but only
  through the enforced task state machine.

  HARD TENETS: fully-local-first (sync is a purely additive opt-in overlay; the
  core task-loader NEVER imports a concrete provider — only the SyncProvider
  interface type + a registry lookup; a missing/failed/un-authed provider never
  degrades local CRUD). The local YAML store is CANONICAL — on conflict, local
  wins; a remote change applies ONLY when the implied transition is legal
  (assertTransition), else it surfaces as a conflict, never forced. A pull
  NEVER writes raw: reconcile() produces a pure plan, sync-layer applies it
  exclusively via updateTask/completeTask/shelveTask, so enforcement + settlement
  fire identically. `link` is NOT a provider method — linking is a pure local
  write (updateTask with external_ref).

  provider.ts defines SyncProvider / ProviderCapabilities / PushResult /
  RemoteState / ExternalRef (pull/reopen/edit are optional, gated by
  capabilities). registry.ts is an id→factory map. claimant-projection.ts is
  Loid's outbound rule (human→assignee; archetype/peer→unassigned + marker
  label). providers/github.ts is the only implemented provider (two-way via
  `gh` CLI). reconcile.ts is the pure inbound brain. sync-layer.ts is the
  executor (outbound projectTransition + inbound apply-through-enforced-writers).
components:
  sync-provider:
    description: Provider-agnostic two-way task-sync seam — SyncProvider interface (push/comment/close/reopen/edit/pull), RemoteState, id→factory registry, Loid's claimant projection
    type: service
    file: provider.ts
    tags: [feature, task-management, sync]
  github-provider:
    description: GitHub SyncProvider (two-way) — gh-CLI shell-out for issue create/comment/close/reopen/edit + pull via `gh issue view --json`; auth via `gh auth status`; self-registers on load
    type: service
    file: providers/github.ts
    tags: [feature, task-management, sync, github]
  task-reconcile:
    description: Pure inbound reconcile brain — compares a local task vs RemoteState and emits a plan (agree/apply/conflict); local canonical, only legal transitions apply, symmetric reopen on remote-open+local-done. No fs/network.
    type: utility
    file: reconcile.ts
    tags: [feature, task-management, sync, task-sync]
  sync-layer:
    description: Two-way sync executor — projectTransition (best-effort outbound push of a transition) + syncTask/syncAllLinked (inbound pull→reconcile→apply ONLY through the enforced updateTask/completeTask/shelveTask writers)
    type: service
    file: sync-layer.ts
    tags: [feature, task-management, sync, task-sync]
